So the trade off is to run until you are at least 2-3 squares
ahead, then alternate firing and running to maintain that lead.
The higher the chance you think you will encounter any other
monster during the run, the farther the lead you want to
maintain.

There's nothing wrong with picking up 10 rocks, moving down
the stairs, throwing several rocks at the mumak, moving up
the stairs.  Keep cycling as long at you weren't hit by the
mumak as soon as you arrived.  It ends up a race between
how fast you heal, how fast the mumak causes damage, how
fast the mumak heals, how much damage your single hits do.
It's times like that when a wand of lightning comes in *very*
handy.


